In article <1993Jan11.204430.12880@cs.cornell.edu>, bau@cs.cornell.edu (David Bau) writes:
> Every time I play, when I get a scroll of ID, I'm always in a conundrum
> when it comes to what order to ID things in.
> 
> Which type of things are the best to ID first?  Which shouldn't you waste
> a scroll IDing?
> 
> David

Depends too much on what you have, what you have identified before and
on your style of playing (sometimes even on your tactical situation) to
give you an unique answer. General rules:
1) ID those items which you can not safely identify by other means.
2) Don't identify items which you may deduce what they are, or are
   useless (typical example: You identified amulet of life saving and
   have poison res. and reflection - don't waste ID on amulets...)
3) When asked what type of items you want to identify - put all types, 
   in the order you need. It could always be one of those 'infinite' 
   ID scrolls and you'll get the chance of knowing the value of your gems...
   For this reason avoid also reading ID scolls if you have only a few 
   unknown items (I hate 'That was all')...
